index 0000000..26e1ddd
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/ops/logging.md
@@ -0,0 +1,84 @@
+# Logging lanes and ops alerts
+
+PegaFila separates observability into three lanes. Pick the lane by asking
+**who needs the information and how quickly they need it** — do not use one
+lane as a substitute for another.
+
+| Lane | Where it goes | Use it for | Do not use it for |
+| --- | --- | --- | --- |
+| **Archive** | `storage/logs/laravel.log` (daily rotation, 14 days) | Routine application logs: debug, info, warnings and errors from normal request/job lifecycles. | Anything that must survive 14 days; anything a person must be paged for. |
+| **Audit** | `storage/logs/audit.log` (daily rotation, 90 days, `info`+) | Durable "who changed what / who tried what" trail: membership/role changes, subscription transitions, login lockouts, privileged admin actions. | Debug noise, request traces, or secrets/PII. |
+| **Alert** | Discord incoming webhook (the `App\Ops\DiscordOpsAlert` service) | Actionable production incidents worth waking someone up: a job exhausted its retries, a payment-gateway webhook is failing, a plan limit is blocking an entity. | Routine errors or anything nobody can act on. Discord is **not** a Monolog channel. |
+
+## Decision guide
+
+1. **Is a person expected to act on this now?**
+   - Yes → send an **Alert** with `DiscordOpsAlert`.
+   - No → continue.
+2. **Is it a durable record of an actor doing (or attempting) something meaningful?**
+   - Yes → write to the **Audit** channel.
+   - No → write to the **Archive** lane (the default `Log::` channel).
+3. **Would the same line be useful during normal debugging?**
+   - Yes → it belongs in the archive lane, even if it is an error.
+   - No → it probably should not be logged at all.
+
+### Examples
+
+```php
+// Archive: routine application log, rotated daily.
+Log::warning('Ticket issuance took longer than expected', [
+    'entity_id' => $entity->id,
+    'duration_ms' => 850,
+]);
+
+// Audit: durable who-changed-what trail, rotated for 90 days.
+Log::channel('audit')->info('Subscription status changed', [
+    'actor_id' => auth()->id(),
+    'entity_id' => $entity->id,
+    'from' => 'trialing',
+    'to' => 'active',
+]);
+
+// Alert: an incident worth paging someone.
+app(DiscordOpsAlert::class)->send(
+    title: 'Asaas webhook failed',
+    message: 'The webhook job exhausted its retries.',
+    context: ['queue' => 'asaas-webhooks', 'entity_id' => $entity->id],
+);
+```
+
+## Discord alerts
+
+`App\Ops\DiscordOpsAlert` is a plain, container-resolvable service with one
+public method:
+
+```php
+public function send(string $title, string $message, array $context = []): void
+```
+
+- Configure `DISCORD_WEBHOOK_URL` in `.env`. When it is empty or `null`, the
+  notifier is a silent no-op and makes no HTTP request.
+- The message is `title`, `message`, then one `key=value` line per context
+  entry, truncated to 1800 multibyte characters.
+- Sensitive context keys (`password`, `token`, `secret`, `authorization`,
+  `api_key`/`api-key`/`apikey`, `webhook`) and any value containing a
+  `Bearer <credential>` are redacted. Nested arrays are redacted recursively.
+- Failures never throw: non-2xx responses and transport errors are logged at
+  `error` level with the webhook URL scrubbed from the log.
+- Alerting is an explicit call in code, never a logging channel. Do not add a
+  `discord` channel to `config/logging.php`.
+
+## Configuration
+
+| Key | Default | Purpose |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| `LOG_CHANNEL` | `stack` | Default Laravel log channel. |
+| `LOG_STACK` | `daily` | Channels in the default stack. |
+| `LOG_LEVEL` | `debug` | Archive channel minimum level. |
+| `LOG_DAILY_DAYS` | `14` | Archive retention in days. |
+| `LOG_AUDIT_LEVEL` | `info` | Audit channel minimum level. |
+| `LOG_AUDIT_DAYS` | `90` | Audit retention in days. |
+| `DISCORD_WEBHOOK_URL` | empty | Discord incoming webhook; empty disables alerts. |
+
+Keep the webhook URL secret: it embeds the webhook token. Never log it, commit
+it, or send it to the browser.
